# Matrix Manual Edit Decision

## Current Model

On 2026-05-29 Juno Castillo admitted she **manually edited** the working **weekend coverage matrix** — the Storm Surge Weekend Coverage Matrix — to **3 deckhands** per pier after May 24 weekend no-shows, citing volunteer pool realism. Priya Nandakumar was not looped on the change; her official **source notes** still roster **4 deckhands** per pier. Marcus Holt built the sailing grid against Juno's three-headcount version and needs reconciliation before the May 31 drill weekend.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-29-coverage-matrix-drift` - Juno admits she **manually edited** the working **weekend coverage matrix** to **3 deckhands** per pier after May 24 no-shows; Priya states official **source notes** still say **4 deckhands** and she was not looped; Marcus notes sailing grid built against Juno's 3-headcount version needing reconciliation before May 31 drill.

## Use In Work

- Treat Juno's 3-deckhand working matrix as operational reality for Marcus Holt's sailing grid, but flag the drift whenever staffing numbers appear in compliance or passenger-facing contexts.
- Loop Priya Nandakumar before attaching the edited matrix to the SSB-DRILL after-action review or publishing headcount externally.

## Limits

This decision records the manual edit only — it does not change Priya's official 4-deckhand source notes or the 45-minute life-vest spot check interval. Simulation weekend dates (May 24, May 31, Jun 7) are governed separately.

## Connections

- [[plan-storm-surge-coverage-matrix]] - Drifted standing plan whose working copy Juno hand-edited to 3 deckhands.
- [[priya-nandakumar]] - Safety lead whose official source notes still specify 4 deckhands and who was not looped on the edit.
- [[juno-castillo]] - Operator who owns the working coverage matrix and admitted the manual change.
- [[ssb-drill]] - Parent drill series whose simulation weekends this matrix staffs.
