# Contractor Staging Access Rule

## Current Model

**Cal Donner** logged an **unauthorized vehicle** — a white panel van with no contractor decal — inside **Pier 9 staging** west apron on **2026-05-07**. The van had an expired out-of-state temp commercial plate matching neither Turnstile Dynamics nor Bridgeway Hoist vendor lists. Fatima Okonkwo revoked the plate; Cal was asked to drop a cone line and photograph the scene for Victor Dunn's incident folder. Night harbormaster logs now treat unmatched vehicles in **pier 9 staging** as immediate escalation items.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-07-pier9-staging-intrusion` - Cal Donner reports white panel van parked inside **pier 9 staging** west apron with no contractor decal, engine off, nobody around — logged as **unauthorized vehicle**; temp commercial plate out-of-state not matching Turnstile or Bridgeway lists; Fatima revokes plate; Cal asked to cone-line and photo for Victor Dunn incident folder.

## Use In Work

- Cross-check vehicles entering Pier 9 staging against Turnstile Dynamics and Bridgeway Hoist badge lists before granting apron access — escalate unmatched plates to Cal Donner and Fatima Okonkwo immediately.
- Reference Victor Dunn's incident folder when reviewing P9-GATE or P9-GANG staging map revisions after unauthorized access events.

## Limits

This incident established staging vigilance for Pier 9 west apron only — not Pier 7 quiet hours, Pier 3 dive inspection overtime, or the 14-badge P9-GATE batch issued 2026-05-11. Cone-line and photo protocol applies to night-staging intrusions Cal Donner discovers.

## Connections

- [[cal-donner]] - Night Harbormaster who discovered and logged the unauthorized vehicle.
- [[pier-9]] - Pier whose staging apron was breached by the unauthorized van.
- [[rel-cal-night-operations]] - Relationship linking Cal to after-hours Pier 9 lighting and staging rules with Juno.
